  "body": "## What changed\n\n`assets/posts/mazak.cps` started the spindle with `MOTON S..` and stopped it with `MOTOFF`. Those are multi-letter words outside RS-274 / ISO 6983, and no public document gives them. `MOTON` also states no spindle direction ahead of a G84 right-hand rigid tap. The post now writes:\n\n- `S<rpm> M3` to start the spindle (in the same place as before: after `T.. M6` / `G43 H..`, before coolant and the first move);\n- `S<rpm> M4` for a left-hand-cut mill (`PARAM MillSpindle reverse`, #988). The post now declares `millSpindleReverse = true` like `fanuc.cps`, and the direction resets at each `OperationName`;\n- `M5` at every section end and in a touch probe's preamble.\n\nThe refusal message for a tap with no spindle start now names `S.. M3`. `assets/posts/AGENTS.md` and the test comments no longer mention MOTON/MOTOFF. No other built-in post wrote these words. The decision is recorded in `docs/decisions/1411-mazak-iso-spindle.md`.\n\nBefore / after (`tap_plate.nc`):\n```diff\n-MOTON S500\n+S500 M3\n ...\n-MOTOFF\n+M5\n```\n\n## Goldens\n\n27 Mazak goldens change, and only on the spindle lines: `MOTON S<n>` became `S<n> M3` and `MOTOFF` became `M5`. Across all `.nc` files the diff has 29 `-MOTOFF`/`+M5` pairs plus the matching `MOTON S<n>`/`S<n> M3` pairs, and no other line changes.\n- `crates/app/tests/golden/nc/mazak/*.nc` (17 files)\n- `crates/app/tests/golden/nc/inch/mazak/{contour_plate_with_hole,drill_peck}.nc`\n- `crates/app/tests/golden/nc/synth_mazak.nc`\n- `crates/post/tests/recorded/golden/mazak/{arcs,drill_retract,empty_section,extreme_coords,full_circle,full_circle_raw,probe}.nc`\n\n## How tested\n\nNew pinning tests are in `crates/post/tests/mazak_spindle_words.rs`:\n- `a_rigid_tap_meets_a_spindle_started_clockwise_and_the_section_ends_m5`\n- `a_left_hand_cut_mill_starts_m4_and_the_next_section_m3_again`\n- `no_mazak_program_carries_the_multi_letter_spindle_words`: the posted program and every recorded Mazak golden are letter+number words only.\n\nTargeted runs, all green:\n- camcraft-post: mazak_spindle_words, script_mazak, probe_spindle, probe_spindle_stop, probe_dialects, arc_planes, cycle_hop, vertical_arc_entry, inverted_post, fanuc_post, comp_plane, comp, comment_escape.\n- camcraft-app: every suite that mentions Mazak or reads the NC goldens, 18 binaries: after_op, conformance, control_comp, post_cycle_feed_spindle, post_spindle_rule_all, post_unit_word, probe_no_coolant, program_comments, program_entry, program_info, program_units, smoothing, wear_comp, thread_passes, posting, recorded_post_streams, rigid_tapping, golden_cl.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-post --all-targets -- -D warnings` is clean.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- The output has not been run on a real Mazak control. It is pinned by the tests and byte-exact goldens only.\n- The full `cargo xtask gate quick` plan was not run: it covers every post and app suite. The targeted set above stood in for it.\n- Clippy was not run on camcraft-app, whose changes are test strings only.\n\nChangelog: Mazak post starts the spindle with `S.. M3` (`M4` for a left-hand-cut mill) and stops it with `M5` instead of `MOTON`/`MOTOFF` (#1411)\n\nEffort: high (no escalation)\n\nFixes #1411\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
